   "major_issues": [
    "The machine’s peak-finishing capacity is never quantified. The q4 share says it “can process all of the hospital’s peak finishing load,” when the known load is only the 960-hour baseline; q6 then assumes build NPV remains $1.64M at the 1,200-hour revised load and recommends a commitment to any peak share above 73.6%. Those conclusions require the machine to cover at least the additional 400 hours at 75%, and the open-ended “above 73.6%” recommendation also requires an upper capacity limit. No such capacity input is available. Thus the pivotal build comparison and robustness recommendation are not verifiable from candidate-visible facts.",
